window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-b7093e7123a14410"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"create-a-classroom-materials-pack\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">制作课堂材料包</h1> <p>制作彼此匹配的教学、练习和家庭沟通材料。</p> <p>使用 ChatGPT，根据经审核的课程演示文稿、单元计划、学校指导、讲义，以及无障碍或语言要求，制作教师指南、学生讲义、答案、家庭概览和材料清单。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要为已审核课程配套材料的教师。</li> <li>要求不同文件中的术语、示例、时间安排和说明保持一致的材料包。</li> <li>需要标出无障碍、翻译或政策审核事项的材料。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>google-drive</code></td> <td>收集经审核的演示文稿、单元计划、学校指导和现有材料。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>制作一致、可编辑的课堂材料和家庭材料。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>制作课堂材料包</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请根据此文件夹中经审核的课程演示文稿和单元计划，制作一套相互配套的课堂材料：\n\n- 教师指南\n- 学生讲义\n- 答案\n- 一页式家庭概览\n- 材料清单\n\n确保所有文件中的术语、示例、时间安排和说明保持一致。请使用我提供的学校指导和现有材料。标出需要进行无障碍、翻译或政策审核的内容。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"set-a-shared-source-of-truth\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">确定共同的权威来源</h2> <p>从经审核的课程演示文稿和单元计划开始。补充当前的学校指导、现有讲义、无障碍要求和语言需求。</p> <p>告诉 ChatGPT 哪些文件决定术语、示例、时间安排和教学判断。</p> <p><a id=\"create-the-companion-materials\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">创建配套材料</h2> <p>使用起始提示词生成一套相互配合的材料：</p> <ol> <li>教师指南，说明准备工作和课堂引导方法。</li> <li>与课程顺序一致的学生讲义。</li> <li>与讲义内容完全对应的答案。</li> <li>使用恰当语言编写的简明家庭概览。</li> <li>材料和准备工作清单。</li> </ol> <p>请它在起草后比较这些文件，并报告术语、示例、说明或答案之间的不一致。</p> <p><a id=\"review-each-audience-separately\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">分别审核每类读者所用的材料</h2> <p>教师应审核教学准确性和可用性。检查学生材料是否清晰、无障碍；答案是否准确对应；与家庭沟通的内容是否符合政策和语言要求。</p> <p>保持所有文件可编辑，并在负责的教师批准整套材料之前清楚标记为草稿。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"create-a-classroom-materials-pack\">Create a classroom materials pack</h1> <p>Produce aligned teaching, practice, and family materials.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT with a reviewed lesson deck, unit plan, school guidance, handouts, and accessibility or language requirements to create a teacher guide, student handout, answer key, family overview, and materials checklist.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Teachers who need companion materials for a reviewed lesson.</li> <li>Packs where terminology, examples, timing, and instructions must agree.</li> <li>Materials that need accessibility, language, or policy review flags.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>google-drive</code></td> <td>Gather the reviewed deck, unit plan, school guidance, and existing materials.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>Create consistent, editable classroom and family materials.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Create a Classroom Materials Pack</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Using the reviewed lesson deck and unit plan in this folder, create a coordinated classroom materials pack:\n\n- teacher guide\n- student handout\n- answer key\n- one-page family overview\n- materials checklist\n\nKeep terminology, examples, timing, and directions consistent across every file. Use the school guidance and existing materials I provide. Flag anything that needs accessibility, translation, or policy review.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"set-a-shared-source-of-truth\">Set a shared source of truth</h2> <p>Start with the reviewed lesson deck and unit plan. Add current school guidance, existing handouts, accessibility requirements, and language needs.</p> <p>Tell ChatGPT which files control terminology, examples, timing, and instructional decisions.</p> <h2 id=\"create-the-companion-materials\">Create the companion materials</h2> <p>Use the starter prompt to generate a coordinated set:</p> <ol> <li>A teacher guide with preparation and facilitation notes.</li> <li>A student handout aligned to the lesson sequence.</li> <li>An answer key that matches the handout exactly.</li> <li>A concise family overview in appropriate language.</li> <li>A materials and preparation checklist.</li> </ol> <p>Ask ChatGPT to compare the files after drafting and report mismatched vocabulary, examples, directions, or answers.</p> <h2 id=\"review-each-audience-separately\">Review each audience separately</h2> <p>Teachers should review instructional accuracy and usability. Check student materials for clarity and accessibility, answer keys for exact alignment, and family communication for policy and language requirements.</p> <p>Keep every file editable and visibly in draft until the responsible educator approves the full pack.</p>"};
